--
-- WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, AND WHY A SCHEMA-ONLY BASELINE IS NOT A RESTORE HERE.
-- Measured, not assumed. Replaying the migration chain onto a catalogue-derived
-- baseline that carried the schema and no rows, migration
--   20260904024105_wapolicy_02_intent_catalogue_and_platform_rules
-- failed with
--   insert or update on table "policy_rule" violates foreign key constraint
--   "policy_rule_rule_type_fkey"
-- and 20260904025050_wapolicy_04_close_default_grants then failed after it,
-- because the object the first one would have created did not exist. Two of the
-- 55 forward migrations, one root cause: this system keeps its vocabulary in
-- TABLES, migrations INSERT against that vocabulary, and a schema-only restore
-- has none of it. A restore without this file looks complete and fails on the
-- next migration that names a rule type.
--
-- WHAT IS IN HERE, AND WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT.
-- In: shipped product vocabulary — reason codes, state models, units,
-- jurisdictions, capability catalogue, provider capability. It is the same for
-- every dealership and is seeded by migrations today.
-- NOT in: `tenants` (the dealership's own identity), `workflow_registry` (real
-- n8n workflow ids, trigger detail and is_active flags — CLAUDE.md calls that
-- operational configuration, not shipped vocabulary, and it is the subject of a
-- known tenancy finding), and every tenant-scoped table. A restore gets no
-- dealership data from this repository, by design.
--
-- ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING throughout: this is safe to re-run and will not
-- overwrite a value an operator has since changed.

